%N A091270 Smallest number having in binary representation a prefix of length n that is also a suffix of its successor.
%H A091270 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A091270/b091270.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A091270 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Binary.html">Binary</a>.
%H A091270 <a href="/index/Bi#binary">Index entries for sequences related to binary expansion of n</a>.
%H A091270 <a href="/index/Rec#order_02">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,-2).
%F A091270 A091269(a(n)) = n and A091269(m) < n for m < a(n).
%F A091270 a(n) = 2^(n+1) - 3 for n > 2 (cf. A036563).
%F A091270 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Aug 26 2026: (Start)
%F A091270 G.f.: x*(2 - x + 2*x^2)/((1 - x)*(1 - 2*x)).
%F A091270 E.g.f.: 1 + x + 2*exp(2*x) - 3*exp(x).
%F A091270 a(n) = 3*a(n-1) - 2*a(n-2) for n > 3. (End)
%t A091270 Join[{0, 2}, 2^Range[3, 35] - 3] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Mar 11 2026 *)
%t A091270 (* Alternative: *)
%t A091270 LinearRecurrence[{3, -2}, {0, 2, 5, 13}, 35] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Mar 11 2026 *)
%Y A091270 Cf. A007088, A036563, A091269.
%K A091270 nonn,base,easy,changed
%O A091270 0,2
